\par\par \b \uc2 EXCHANGE --- Workers Vote to Authorize Strike at Big 3 Automakers\b0\par\par\uc2 By Will Feuer \par \uc2 415 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 August 2023\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B9\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Workers at the Detroit automakers voted overwhelmingly in favor of a measure that authorizes the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  leadership to call for a strike as talks between the union and companies continue.\par \par \uc2 Final votes are still being tabulated, the union said, but the current combined average across the Big Three automakers was 97% in favor of strike authorization.\par \par \uc2 The strike-authorization vote is a procedural step that enables union leadership to initiate a work stoppage. It doesn't guarantee a strike will be called.\par \par \uc2 "Our union's membership is clearly fed up with living paycheck-to-paycheck while the corporate elite and billionaire class continue to make out like bandits," said the \uc2 UAW\uc2 's newly elected president, Shawn Fain. "The Big Three have been breaking the bank while we have been breaking our backs."\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  is negotiating new four-year labor agreements for about 146,000 U.S. hourly workers at \uc2 General Motors\uc2 , \uc2 Ford Motor\uc2  and \uc2 Jeep\uc2 -maker \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 . The existing contracts expire on Sept. 14.\par \par \uc2 "We look forward to working with the \uc2 UAW\uc2  on creative solutions during this time when our dramatically changing industry needs a skilled and competitive workforce more than ever," Ford said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 GM\uc2  said the company continues to bargain in good faith. \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  didn't immediately respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 The union is seeking to regain benefits lost in previous rounds of talks and increase wages by at least 40% during the life of the next contract, a boost that would be the largest in recent memory.\par \par \uc2 The negotiations have turned contentious, with \uc2 UAW\uc2  leadership calling out slow progress. Earlier this month, Fain criticized \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  for demanding concessions at the bargaining table that he described as a "slap in the face" to workers.\par \par \uc2 Union members have been practicing picketing this week, and Fain has said that if the companies don't change the way negotiations are going, they should expect a strike.\par \par \uc2 "Our message to the Big Three is simple: record profits mean record contracts," Fain said Thursday in a letter to the union's members.\par \par \uc2 The negotiations are among a wave of protracted labor talks this year that have vexed companies and at times threatened to spill over into work stoppages. The \uc2 International Brotherhood of Teamsters\uc2  recently reached a five-year contract agreement with \uc2 United Parcel Service\uc2 , dodging a potential standoff that could have rippled across the U.S. supply chain.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020230826ej8q0002r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
89
