\par\par \b \uc2 Business News: \uc2 UAW\uc2  to Vote on Strike Approval As Talks With Carmakers Stall\b0\par\par\uc2 By Nora Eckert \par \uc2 495 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 August 2023\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  said Tuesday labor negotiations with the Detroit automakers have been sluggish and the union would hold a strike authorization vote next week, a procedural step needed for its leadership to call a work stoppage.\par \par \uc2 "Today marks 30 days until the union's contract with the Big Three expires, but bargaining at all three tables has yet to progress beyond noneconomic issues," the union said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  is negotiating new four-year labor agreements for about 146,000 U.S. hourly workers at \uc2 General Motors\uc2 , \uc2 Ford Motor\uc2  and Jeep maker \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 . The existing contracts expire on Sept. 14.\par \par \uc2 A strike authorization vote is an action that typically takes place before the labor agreements expire and gives the union the option of calling a strike if leaders see fit. The union requires at least two-thirds of voting members to back the authorization to move forward, a bar that it has easily passed in the past.\par \par \uc2 Union officials say this doesn't guarantee a strike will happen and it will depend on how negotiations unfold in coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2  President Shawn Fain, during a live stream event Tuesday, said he doesn't plan to extend the contracts past the expiration date, a move that the union has sometimes allowed in the past to continue talks without a strike.\par \par \uc2 "The choice is yours about what happens next," Fain said, addressing the Detroit companies. "Either stop dragging your feet in negotiations, or be prepared to strike."\par \par \uc2 GM\uc2  takes its responsibility to support employees seriously, and is bargaining in good faith to reach an agreement, a \uc2 GM\uc2  spokesman said. Ford declined to comment. \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  didn't respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 Analysts have warned the probability of a walkout is higher this year in part because the union has struck a more militant tone and entered into talks with a list of demands that are far more aggressive than in previous rounds of bargaining.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2 's strike fund, which provides members on walkout with a $500-a-week payment, is at more than $825 million, the union said.\par \par \uc2 The negotiations this time around have led to more public clashes between the two sides, with Fain vocal about his frustration with the companies and the automakers speaking openly about their intentions and gripes.\par \par \uc2 The change-minded \uc2 UAW\uc2  leader was elected in March and quickly threw out the traditional union playbook. He ditched the typical handshake with automotive executives to kick off labor talks and instead, shook hands with members while visiting unionized plants.\par \par \uc2 As negotiations have progressed, he has bashed specific proposals from the companies in a more public way than past union heads have. Last week, Fain threw a copy of proposals \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  made in a trash can.\par \par \uc2 The union's demands include a more than 40% pay hike for workers and the return of cost-of-living adjustments.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020230816ej8g0001o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
