\par\par \b \uc2 Business News: Emmy Awards Postponed Amid Hollywood Strikes --- Show that honors prime-time TV will now air on Jan. 15, instead of September\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 370 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 August 2023\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B5\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Emmy Awards have been postponed until January amid a historic work stoppage in show business, with screen actors and writers on strike because of contract battles with major studios.\par \par \uc2 The show honoring achievements in prime-time television will air on Jan. 15 -- months after its originally scheduled broadcast of Sept. 18,the Television Academy and Fox said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The rescheduled show will fall on Martin Luther King Jr. Day. Fox will broadcast the show from Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 The Creative Arts Emmy Awards, which was originally scheduled for Sept. 9-10, will take place Jan. 6-7 in Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 Members of the Writers Guild of America began their strike May 2 -- just over 100 days ago. Members of the Screen Actors Guild joined them on the picket lines in July.\par \par \uc2 The unions are pushing for higher pay, increased residuals and protections against the use of artificial intelligence in the creative process.\par \par \uc2 The strike rules create a challenge for organizers of these industry awards. Writers who create the material used by hosts and presenters are forbidden under union rules from participating in the telecast during the strike. Actors are also barred by union rules from promoting the work of studios they are striking against and from accepting trophies on national television.\par \par \uc2 It is unclear when the disputes will be resolved.\par \par \uc2 Nominees for the 75th annual Primetime Emmy Awards were unveiled in July, just before the \uc2 Screen Actors Guild\uc2  joined striking writers on the picket line.\par \par \uc2 "Succession," which ended its fourth and final season on \uc2 HBO\uc2  this year, led the nominations with 27 nods, including in top categories like best drama, best actor and best actress. "The Last of Us" earned 24 nominations, "The White Lotus" received 23 and "Ted Lasso" got 21.\par \par \uc2 The delay comes after the Tony Awards aired in June during the writers strike. Playwrights convinced the Writers Guild of America that a disruption could hurt business on Broadway.\par \par \uc2 The show, hosted by Academy Award winner Ariana DeBose, aired without scripted segments.\par \par \uc2 Many presenters and winners showed solidarity with the writers.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020230811ej8b00014\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
