\par\par \uc2 The Property Report\par \b \uc2 Zoom, Others Call Staff Back to Office\b0\par\par\uc2 By Chip Cutter \par \uc2 399 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 August 2023\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B6\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Some of the pioneers of the work-from-home movement are ordering employees back to the office for at least part of the week, in another sign the era of remote work is evolving.\par \par \uc2 Among the latest to reverse course is the technology company Zoom, maker of the videoconferencing software that became ubiquitous during the pandemic. Executives in recent days have told employees that they see value in staffers working with their teams in-person, and that the company would begin requiring people who live near its offices to work on-site two days a week.\par \par \uc2 "We believe that a structured hybrid approach -- meaning employees that live near an office need to be on-site two days a week to interact with their teams -- is most effective for Zoom," a spokeswoman said in a statement. "Additionally, we will continue to hire the best talent, regardless of location."\par \par \uc2 Zoom's hybrid work model applies to employees who live within about 50 miles of a company office, the spokeswoman said, and it will take effect in August and September. Insider earlier reported on Zoom's new mandate.\par \par \uc2 Other companies have changed return-to-office policies in recent months. \uc2 Meta Platforms\uc2  workers assigned to an office will need to come in three days a week starting in September, as part of a more structured hybrid schedule, the company said in June. \uc2 Meta\uc2  said at the time that the mandate only applies to workers already in an office some days, and doesn't apply to workers who have remote positions.\par \par \uc2 Alphabet\uc2 -owned \uc2 Google\uc2  sent a companywide email in June telling workers that office attendance would begin to factor into performance reviews. \uc2 Google\uc2  requires most employees to be in the office three days a week.\par \par \uc2 The online-dating platform \uc2 Grindr\uc2  told employees that it would implement a hybrid work model requiring them to work in an office two days a week beginning in October. \uc2 Grindr\uc2  CEO George Arison said last week that the company is no longer "remote first" and that a hybrid schedule would provide flexibility while allowing for greater collaboration, in a memo viewed by The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Employees at \uc2 Grindr\uc2  who don't live within commuting distance of a designated company office will need to relocate, with the company offering relocation assistance, or accept a severance package.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020230809ej890001i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
