\par\par \b \uc2 Business News: \uc2 UPS\uc2 , Teamsters Avert Strike With Pact --- Five-year deal valued at $30 billion settles contentious talks with drivers, sorters\b0\par\par\uc2 By Esther Fung \par \uc2 388 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 July 2023\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 United Parcel Service\uc2  and the \uc2 International Brotherhood of Teamsters\uc2  have reached an agreement on a five-year labor contract, preventing a potential strike by roughly 330,000 package delivery drivers and package sorters.\par \par \uc2 The labor union said the contract was worth around $30 billion overall. The agreement still has to be ratified by employees.\par \par \uc2 "This contract sets a new standard in the labor movement and raises the bar for all workers," \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  General President Sean O'Brien said.\par \par \uc2 The UPS-Teamsters contract is the largest collective-bargaining agreement involving a private employer in North America, and a strike could harm the supply chains of many companies. \uc2 UPS\uc2  moves approximately 5% of the nation's gross domestic product -- or roughly $3.8 billion of goods every day, according to the \uc2 U.S. Chamber of Commerce\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 President Biden on Tuesday congratulated the union and company on working out their differences at the bargaining table.\par \par \uc2 A dispute that was holding up negotiations in recent weeks was over wages for part-time workers. The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  were seeking an hourly wage for part-time workers north of $20.\par \par \uc2 Under the agreement, \uc2 UPS\uc2  would pay new part-time workers a wage of $21 an hour, the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  said. Currently, starting part-time hourly wages are $16.20 and could be higher in places where there is more competition for labor.\par \par \uc2 Existing workers would get a $2.75-an-hour raise this year, and $7.50 more per hour over the remainder of the contract. Workers' wages rose roughly $5.30 an hour in the five-year deal that runs through July 31.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, the company and union each accused the other of walking away from contract talks, which have been under way since May.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 -represented workers voted to authorize a strike if a new agreement wasn't reached.\par \par \uc2 "This agreement continues to reward \uc2 UPS\uc2 's full- and part-time employees with industry-leading pay and benefits while retaining the flexibility we need to stay competitive, serve our customers and keep our business strong," said \uc2 UPS\uc2  Chief Executive \uc2 Carol Tome\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Shares in \uc2 UPS\uc2  surged briefly after media reports about the agreement but closed down 1.9% on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020230726ej7q00020\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
