\par\par \b \uc2 EXCHANGE --- Binance Lays Off Over 1,000 Employees\b0\par\par\uc2 By Patricia Kowsmann and Caitlin Ostroff \par \uc2 472 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 July 2023\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Binance\uc2 , the giant crypto exchange, is cutting a big chunk of its workforce during a federal crackdown in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Over 1,000 people have been fired in recent weeks, according to a person familiar with the moves.\par \par \uc2 The exercise, which is continuing, could result in \uc2 Binance\uc2  losing more than a third of its staff, the person said.\par \par \uc2 More employees were laid off this week, according to former employees, who said customer-service workers were heavily affected. The cuts were global, including about three dozen customer-service employees in India.\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal has reported layoffs and resignations were taking place, including in the U.S., but the scope of the cuts weren't known.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Binance\uc2  spokesman confirmed employees were being let go but declined to say how many.\par \par \uc2 "As we prepare for the next major bull cycle, it has become clear that we need to focus on talent density across the organization to ensure we remain nimble and dynamic. This is not a case of right sizing, but rather, re-evaluating whether we have the right talent and expertise in critical roles," he said.\par \par \uc2 Before the layoffs, \uc2 Binance\uc2  had a global staff of 8,000.\par \par \uc2 The exchange has been the target of a series of actions by U.S. regulators over the past months as they try to control an industry that for long ran loose.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  sued the company and its founder, \uc2 Changpeng Zhao\uc2 , in June. It alleges they illegally operated in the country and misused customer funds, among other things.\par \par \uc2 Binance\uc2  has denied the allegations.\par \par \uc2 The exchange has also faced setbacks in Europe as it tries to get licenses to operate.\par \par \uc2 The biggest challenge for the exchange, however, is a continuing investigation by the Justice Department.\par \par \uc2 The Journal reported last week that \uc2 Binance\uc2  executives have grown worried that the DOJ will file charges against the firm and Zhao.\par \par \uc2 Zhao has resisted giving up control of the company or stepping aside, and many inside the firm believe his staying could put \uc2 Binance\uc2 's survival into question, the Journal reported.\par \par \uc2 A series of high-profile employees recently left, including the company's general counsel, chief strategy officer and head of investigations.\par \par \uc2 Amid fears of a Justice Department action, the exchange decided to eliminate any physical presence in the U.S., where it is relocating or laying off about 150 people.\par \par \uc2 Binance\uc2  has a separate exchange in the U.S., \uc2 Binance\uc2 . US, whose workforce is separate and which is facing its own challenges. After the SEC lawsuit its market share took a dive.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, \uc2 Binance\uc2  celebrated its six-year anniversary.\par \par \uc2 "We can't wait for what lies ahead," it said in a tweet message.\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 Dave Michaels contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020230715ej7f00031\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
