\par\par \b \uc2 Actors to Join Writers on Strike As Streaming Roils Hollywood\b0\par\par\uc2 By Joe Flint \par \uc2 900 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 July 2023\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Hollywood actors planned to go on strike starting Friday after their union failed to reach a new labor contract with studios, joining already-striking writers in a standoff likely to grind the entertainment industry to a halt.\par \par \uc2 A prolonged strike involving writers and actors could mean that broadcast and cable networks won't have fresh scripted TV episodes ready for the early fall, and that Hollywood's pipeline of fresh shows and movies will thin.\par \par \uc2 Streamers such as \uc2 Netflix\uc2  and Max tend to produce programming far in advance of planned release dates, as do movie studios, so they might not feel the effect of a labor stoppage until late 2024 at the earliest.\par \par \uc2 The talks between the Screen Actors Guild -- American Federation of Television and Radio Artists and the \uc2 Alliance of Motion Picture and Television Producers\uc2 , a coalition representing movie and TV studios, networks and streamers, ended Wednesday night as the deadline to reach a new three-year deal expired.\par \par \uc2 The strike also affects the promotion of work already shot. As "\uc2 Oppenheimer\uc2 " premiered in London Thursday, director Christopher Nolan informed audience members that the movie's stars, including Cillian Murphy and Emily Blunt, had walked out of the premiere event, according to a video posted on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Issues that have led writers and actors to this point include compensation, royalties and the use of artificial intelligence during the creative process.\par \par \uc2 At a news conference Thursday, \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  President Fran Drescher said she couldn't believe how far apart the two sides were on those key issues.\par \par \uc2 "The entire business model has been changed by streaming, digital, artificial intelligence," Drescher said. "If we don't stand tall right now, we are all going to be in trouble. We are all going to be in jeopardy of being replaced by machines and big business."\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 SAG\uc2  strike against the sellers of content is its first in nearly four decades and the first time since 1960 that both writers and performers have been on the picket line at the same time. The Writers Guild of America put their pens down on May 2.\par \par \uc2 In a recent statement to members, \uc2 SAG\uc2 , which represents about 140,000 actors as well as stunt performers and voice-over artists, said residual payments aren't keeping up with the revenue media companies are generating from scripted content around the globe.\par \par \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  chief negotiator Duncan Crabtree-Ireland said the union sought a 2% cut of streaming subscription revenues for performers, which was a nonstarter for the \uc2 AMPTP\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Generative artificial intelligence is another sticking point, with writers and actors seeking strict guidelines and protections over the use of the technology. There is concern that generative AI could be used to supplant writers. Performers fear unauthorized use of their likeness without their consent or compensation.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 AMPTP\uc2  said Thursday its offer to \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  included the biggest increase to minimum payments in 35 years, as well as a 76% increase for most streaming foreign residuals.\par \par \uc2 With regards to AI, the \uc2 AMPTP\uc2  said it proposed safeguards to protect performers' digital likenesses, including "a requirement for performer's consent for the creation and use of digital replicas or for digital alterations of a performance."\par \par \uc2 The strike will have an adverse effect on the Los Angeles economy, and the shutdown of productions will hit thousands of other workers and businesses that serve the industry.\par \par \uc2 For the major entertainment giants, a dual strike comes at an already challenging time. Several major streaming services including Walt Disney's Disney+ and \uc2 Paramount Global\uc2 's Paramount+ are unprofitable, and a weak advertising market and cord-cutting are inflicting pain on the traditional television businesses that had buoyed them.\par \par \uc2 "The strikes will create even more chaos," said MoffettNathanson media analyst \uc2 Michael Nathanson\uc2 , adding that the industry is "seeing declines in linear profitability and no signs of true sustainable profitability in streaming."\par \par \uc2 Since the writers walked out, much of the industry has been on a forced hiatus. Episodes for new and returning television shows aren't being written and late-night shows such as ABC's "Jimmy Kimmel Live!" are dark.\par \par \uc2 Performers were continuing to work on movies and television shows with completed scripts, although striking writers often targeted active productions and managed to even temporarily shut several down.\par \par \uc2 With performers on strike as well, work is only likely to continue on content that is in the final stages of post production, in which actors and writers aren't typically required.\par \par \uc2 Moments after the strike was officially announced, actress Jamie Lee Curtis, a recent guest star on season 2 of FX's "The Bear," posted an image of comedy/tragedy theater masks on \uc2 Instagram\uc2  and wrote, "It looks like it's time to take down the masks and pick up the signs."\par \par \uc2 On \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , "Frozen" actor Josh Gad wrote, "The LA styrofoam and cardboard industry is about to have an even busier summer."\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, the Fox network announced its fall schedule would be mostly composed of unscripted fare and animated shows that had already finished production before the strikes.\par \par \uc2 Hollywood's other major union -- the \uc2 Directors Guild of America\uc2  -- agreed to a new deallast month that provided for a 21% increase in royalties from streaming services, a significant portion of which will come from international operations.\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 Ashley Wong contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020230714ej7e0002a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
