\par\par \b \uc2 Business News: \uc2 UPS\uc2 , Union Hit Snag in Labor Talks\b0\par\par\uc2 By Esther Fung \par \uc2 598 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 July 2023\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 United Parcel Service\uc2  and the \uc2 International Brotherhood of Teamsters\uc2  said negotiations have stalled on a new labor contract, raising the risk of roughly 330,000 package-delivery drivers and package sorters going on strike next month.\par \par \uc2 The company and union on Wednesday each accused the other of walking away from contract talks, which have been under way since May. The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 -represented workers voted to authorize a strike if a new agreement isn't reached. The current deal expires July 31.\par \par \uc2 The UPS-Teamsters contract is the largest collective-bargaining agreement involving a private employer in North America, and a strike could harm the supply chains of many companies. \uc2 UPS\uc2  pilots, airline and ground mechanics and some other employees are covered under different labor contracts. "The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  have stopped negotiating despite \uc2 UPS\uc2 's historic offer that builds on our industry-leading pay," \uc2 UPS\uc2  spokesman Jim Mayer said. "We have nearly a month left to negotiate. We have not walked away, and the union has a responsibility to remain at the table."\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  said the company's most recent offer was unacceptable and didn't address their members' needs. No additional negotiations have been scheduled, according to the union. Last week, the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  said there hasn't been an agreement on prospective wage increases and cost-of-living adjustments for workers.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 UPS\uc2  had a choice to make, and they have clearly chosen to go down the wrong road," said \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  General President Sean O'Brien.\par \par \uc2 Terms of the latest offer that \uc2 UPS\uc2  made to the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  couldn't be learned.\par \par \uc2 UPS\uc2  full-time package-delivery drivers with at least four years in the company make an average of $42 an hour, or about $95,000 annually. The union said that workers need more compensation for working through the pandemic and for forced overtime during that period.\par \par \uc2 The hourly wage increase totaled $4.15 over the life of the current UPS-Teamsters agreement, which began in 2018.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  last month secured a new contract for unionized employees with trucking company ABF Freight in which workers would get a $3.50-an-hour raise starting in July. The total increase over five years would be $6.50 an hour. The ABF deal sets a benchmark for expectations for the \uc2 UPS\uc2  contract, said \uc2 Satish Jindel\uc2 , president of \uc2 ShipMatrix\uc2 , which analyzes package-shipping data.\par \par \uc2 Shares in \uc2 UPS\uc2  fell about 2% Wednesday as investors weighed the prospects of a stalemate in labor talks.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  and \uc2 UPS\uc2  have made inroads on other issues, including the company agreeing to eliminate its two-tier system for drivers. The union said this classification had earlier allowed \uc2 UPS\uc2  to pay some drivers lower wages.\par \par \uc2 The parties last month reached an agreement on air conditioning in vehicles, including equipping newly purchased small-package vehicles with cooling capabilities, installing fans in package cars and heat shields on the cargo floor. The union said drivers suffer extreme temperatures and some have succumbed to heat-related injuries during the summer.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  and the company have also agreed on supplemental contracts across the country covering local work rules.\par \par \uc2 In anticipation of a possible work stoppage, some customers of \uc2 UPS\uc2  have started conversations with alternative carriers as part of business continuity plans. Parcel consultants said the closer it gets to the contract deadline, more customers will start shifting parcel volumes to other carriers to mitigate risks to their operations.\par \par \uc2 The last time \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 -represented workers had a walkout at \uc2 UPS\uc2  was in August 1997.\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 Colin Kellaher contributed to this article.\par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw262\pich465\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3930\pichgoal6975
