\par\par \b \uc2 EXCHANGE --- UPS Workers Authorize Strike If Talks Falter\b0\par\par\uc2 By Esther Fung \par \uc2 416 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 June 2023\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B9\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 United Parcel Service\uc2  workers who are represented by the \uc2 International Brotherhood of Teamsters\uc2  voted to authorize a strike if contract negotiations with the company fail to yield a new agreement.\par \par \uc2 The current \uc2 UPS\uc2  contract covers about 330,000 employees, including delivery drivers and package handlers, and expires July 31. The deal was signed in 2018.\par \par \uc2 "The strongest leverage our members have is their labor and they are prepared to withhold it to ensure \uc2 UPS\uc2  acts accordingly," \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  General President Sean M. O'Brien said Friday.\par \par \uc2 The vote tally comes after West Coast dockworkers earlier this week reached a tentative six-year agreement with port employers after more than a year of contentious negotiations. The Biden administration sought to ease tensions between the groups as an impasse threatened to obstruct the movement of goods.\par \par \uc2 In anticipation of a possible work stoppage, some customers of \uc2 UPS\uc2  have already started conversations with alternative carriers. The last time Teamster-represented workers had a walkout at \uc2 UPS\uc2  was in August 1997.\par \par \uc2 "The results do not mean a strike is imminent and do not impact our current business operations in any way," said \uc2 UPS\uc2  spokesman Glenn Zaccara. "Authorization votes and approvals are normal steps in labor union negotiations. \uc2 UPS\uc2  remains confident that we will reach an agreement that provides wins for our employees, the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 , our company and our customers."\par \par \uc2 Current talks between the union and company have been focused on a five-year deal that would run through 2028. In recent weeks, subcommittees between the union and \uc2 UPS\uc2  reached tentative agreements on several issues, including operating priorities, the use of technology and in-vehicle cameras.\par \par \uc2 The parties have also reached an agreement on air conditioning in vehicles, including equipping newly purchased small package vehicles with air conditioning, installing fans in package cars and heat shields on the cargo floor. The union said that drivers suffer extreme temperatures and some have succumbed to heat-related injuries during the summer when vehicles overheat.\par \par \uc2 Other issues still on the bargaining table include higher pay for part-timers and a second category of weekend drivers, which \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  want to do away with. The union has said that a two-tier system of drivers allows \uc2 UPS\uc2  to use lower-paid workers to deliver packages on weekends, curbing delivery costs.\par \par \uc2 UPS\uc2  said that part-time roles are necessary as the nature of parcel delivery work includes alternating bursts of activity and slack time throughout the day.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020230617ej6h0002s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
