\par\par \b \uc2 Patterson-UTI\uc2 , NexTier Strike Agreement to Merge\b0\par\par\uc2 By Dean Seal \par \uc2 469 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 June 2023\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B6\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 NexTier Oilfield Solutions\uc2  and \uc2 Patterson-UTI Energy\uc2  have agreed to an all-stock merger to form a bigger player in the oil-field-services industry with an enterprise value of $5.4 billion.\par \par \uc2 The deal has been approved by the boards of both companies. Once the transaction closes, shareholders of \uc2 Patterson-UTI\uc2  will own about 55% of the new company, while NexTier shareholders will own the remaining 45%.\par \par \uc2 "As one company, we will have a significantly expanded, comprehensive portfolio of oil-field-services offerings across the most active producing basins in the United States, along with operations in Latin America," \uc2 Patterson-UTI\uc2  Chief Executive \uc2 Andy Hendricks\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal reported Monday that the two Houston-based companies were holding talks for a possible tie-up. The oil-field-services industry is becoming more consolidated as it caters to a shrinking pool of oil- and gas-producing clients, which has created the need for fewer but larger providers, according to analysts.\par \par \uc2 Deals in the space have revved up after energy producers pulled in a deluge of cash last year when Russia's invasion of Ukraine sent oil and gas prices to multiyear highs. \uc2 Exxon Mobil\uc2  is on the prowl for a blockbuster deal and has held early acquisition talks with \uc2 Pioneer Natural Resources\uc2 , while \uc2 Chevron\uc2  recently spent more than $6 billion to acquire a rival with sizable operations in Texas and Colorado.\par \par \uc2 Going into their merger, NexTier has a market capitalization of just under $2 billion after its shares dropped roughly 11% over the past 12 months. Shares of \uc2 Patterson-UTI\uc2  have fallen nearly 33% in the same period, giving it a market value of about $2.2 billion.\par \par \uc2 The combined company would operate under the name \uc2 Patterson-UTI Energy\uc2 , trade under Patterson's current ticker symbol, PTEN, and maintain a corporate headquarters in Houston. The company's well-completion business would operate under the NexTier Completions brand.\par \par \uc2 Hendricks is set to take over as the new company's president and chief executive, while \uc2 Robert Drummond\uc2 , who serves in those positions for NexTier, would be installed as vice chair of the combined company's board.\par \par \uc2 The merger will allow \uc2 Patterson-UTI\uc2 , which is largely focused on onshore-drilling services, to get more into fracking. NexTier, which was born out of a 2019 merger between \uc2 C&J Energy Services\uc2  and Keane Group, is a provider of well-completion and production services that doubled its revenue to $3.24 billion last year thanks to higher prices and increased fracking activity.\par \par \uc2 The business combination is expected to start boosting earnings by 2024 and generate about $200 million in annual cost savings and synergies within 18 months after the deal closes. The merger is expected to close in the fourth quarter, pending regulatory approvals.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020230616ej6g00014\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
