\par\par \b \uc2 Business News: Actors Guild Authorizes Strike if Needed\b0\par\par\uc2 By Suryatapa Bhattacharya \par \uc2 301 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 June 2023\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Members of the Screen Actors Guild voted to empower the union to call for a strike if contract negotiations with studios and other power players break down.\par \par \uc2 The vote comes at a tense moment in Hollywood. Thousands of writers have been on strike for more than a month, picketing outside entertainment companies in Los Angeles and New York.\par \par \uc2 That strike could continue into summer, casting a pall over television and film lineups.\par \par \uc2 Nearly 65,000 members of the \uc2 Screen Actors Guild-American Federation of Television and Radio Artists\uc2  cast ballots, with around 98% voting in favor of a strike authorization, the union said Monday.\par \par \uc2 "Together we lock elbows and in unity we build a new contract that honors our contributions in this remarkable industry, reflects the new digital and streaming business model and brings all our concerns for protections and benefits into the now," said actress and \uc2 SAG-Aftra\uc2  President Fran Drescher. In addition to actors, the union's roughly 160,000 members include stunt performers, singers, dancers, radio announcers and puppeteers.\par \par \uc2 SAG-Aftra\uc2  and the \uc2 Alliance of Motion Picture and Television Producers\uc2  are scheduled to start talks on June 7, as part of regular negotiations that occur every three years. The current contract ends June 30.\par \par \uc2 The alliance, whose members include \uc2 Netflix\uc2 , \uc2 Walt Disney\uc2 , \uc2 Warner Bros. Discovery\uc2  and \uc2 Paramount Global\uc2 , said Monday its goal in the talks is to reach a new agreement that is beneficial to union members as well as the industry.\par \par \uc2 "An actor's strike that lingers through summer will likely have more of an effect on content production than a writers' strike, as much of the writing for slated content has been completed," said Jacquie Corbelli, chief executive of \uc2 BrightLine\uc2 , a TV ad tech provider.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020230606ej660001q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
